    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Build succeeds and all tests pass. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: soft-duplicate detection on owner creation\n\nWhen a new owner isn't a hard identity duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a *different* telephone, it's still created and now reports `possibleDuplicate: true` with `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matched owner's id; otherwise `possibleDuplicate: false`.\n\nI followed the existing \"assign step\" pattern used for the other derived owner fields (namesake count, membership level, bulk-signup warning), keeping each piece in its own small unit:\n\n1. **New pipeline step** \u2014 `AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate.java`: reads the built owner and existing owners in the same transaction (before persist, so it isn't matched against itself), finds the earliest existing owner sharing `lastName` (case-insensitive) + `postcode` with a differing telephone, and records the flag/id. A shared postcode is required to match.\n\n2. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`: inserted the `assignPossibleDuplicate` step (under `transaction` governance) between `assignBulkSignupWarning` and `applyRegistrationDate`. Hard duplicates are still rejected upstream by `EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity`, so this only ever flags genuine soft matches.\n\n3. **Entity** \u2014 `Owner.java`: added `possibleDuplicate` (Boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (Integer) columns with accessors.\n\n4. **Schema** \u2014 added `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` columns to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb/h2/postgres/mysql); tests run on hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the DDL had to be explicit.\n\n5. **API contract** \u2014 `openapi.yml`: added the two read-only properties to the `Owner` schema, which regenerates `OwnerDto`; MapStruct auto-maps the same-named entity fields, so the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response carries them with no mapper change needed.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` test and the full suite are green.",
